{# PL·A3 "Where nobody has been" — ABSENCE, NOT ACTIVITY.

   Measured from the last track that ENTERED the zone, not from the last patrol
   that named a station: a patrol names where it set off from and no zone at all,
   so a station's name is not evidence anybody crossed a polygon.

   Zones are the HOST's lens and an org with none is the normal state, so an area
   with no zones drawn says that rather than showing an empty table.

   The two columns read two windows and the footer says which: days-since looks
   over all of history, because a zone nobody has entered for a year is exactly
   the row this card exists for; the coverage share is this month's, so it
   reconciles with the module's own PL·03. Both are the worker's facts, and the
   footer's caption says when they are true as of. #}
{% set pl = by.patrols %}
{% set g = pl.gaps %}
<div class="c" data-w="pl_gaps">
    <span class="tab">Where nobody has been<span class="src">· by zone · worst first</span></span>
    <span class="ao-by"><i></i>patrols</span>

    {% if g.zones|length %}
        <table class="tbl">
            <tr>
                <th>zone</th>
                <th>last patrol entered</th>
                <th class="patrol-right">days since</th>
                <th class="patrol-right">within {{ g.bufferKm|number_format }} km</th>
            </tr>
            {% for z in g.zones %}
                <tr>
                    <td>{{ z.zone }}</td>
                    {# A zone the worker has not measured yet says so, and claims
                       neither a date nor a gap. #}
                    <td class="fog">{% if not z.computed %}not computed yet · runs hourly{% elseif z.lastEnteredAt %}<time datetime="{{ z.lastEnteredAt|date('c') }}" data-localtime-format="date">{{ z.lastEnteredAt|date('D j M')|lower }}</time>{% if z.lastPatrol %} · {{ z.lastPatrol.ref }}{% endif %}{% else %}no track has entered it{% endif %}</td>
                    {# Never is the worst gap there is and has no number, so it
                       wears the failure chip and says the word. #}
                    <td class="num">
                        {% if not z.computed %}
                            —
                        {% elseif z.never %}
                            <span class="chip fail">never</span>
                        {% else %}
                            <span class="chip {{ z.daysSince >= 7 ? 'fail' : (z.daysSince >= 4 ? 'warn' : (z.daysSince >= 1 ? 'idle' : 'ok')) }}">{{ z.daysSince }} d</span>
                        {% endif %}
                    </td>
                    {# An em dash where no track was recorded this month: zero
                       coverage and unknown coverage are different facts. #}
                    <td class="num">{{ z.coverageFraction is null ? '—' : (z.coverageFraction * 100)|round ~ ' %' }}</td>
                </tr>
            {% endfor %}
        </table>

        <div class="rln patrol-ao-foot">
            <span class="fog">Area within {{ g.bufferKm|number_format }} km of a track, this month{{ include('@UhifadhiPatrol/_as_of.html.twig', {fact: g.asOf}, with_context = false) }}</span>
            <span class="mono acc patrol-ao-mono">{{ g.areaCoverageFraction is null ? '—' : (g.areaCoverageFraction * 100)|round ~ ' %' }} · the module’s own number</span>
        </div>
    {% else %}
        <p class="patrol-empty">This area has no zones drawn, so there is nothing to measure absence against. Zones are drawn in the area’s own settings; an area with none is a normal state, not a missing configuration.</p>
    {% endif %}
</div>
